---
description: Un-scramble Hebrew-keyboard-layout gibberish (AGI) before acting on a user message
alwaysApply: true
---

When a user message contains garbled Hebrew characters that don't form real Hebrew
words — English typed while the keyboard was still on a Hebrew layout (e.g. `פודי`
= `push`, `עןא פודי` = `git push`) — recover the intended text before responding:

```bash
node ~/.claude/skills/agi/scripts/agi.mjs "<the garbled text>"
```

Use the output as the user's actual message. It's a deterministic key remap — real
English and genuine Hebrew are left unchanged, so it's a no-op on normal input.
